### UI Builder API Tests

Exercises `/api/ui-builder` (pages, drafts, publishing, visibility, revisions,
the editing lease and published pages) with the VS Code REST Client. Select the
`local` or `deployed` environment; `baseUrl`, `adminUid` and `adminPassword`
are the same variables `toolchain.http` uses, set in the Git-ignored
`.vscode/settings.json`. Never put passwords in this file.

Every signed-in UI Builder route checks that the request comes from an OCS
page (UiBuilderRequestGuard): `X-Origin: client`, an `Origin` listed in
`ui-builder.allowed-origins`, and a JSON body type on writes. Set `pagesOrigin`
below to the site you test from (https://pages.opencodingsociety.com when
deployed).

Run the requests in order: later ones use the page id that request 4 returns.
They write a real page on that environment, so its title says 2099, and the
last requests delete it. A deleted page keeps its slug, so request 9 makes a
new one each run.

@pagesOrigin = http://localhost:4500

### 1. Sign in (the JWT cookie is kept for the requests below)

# @name loginUiBuilder
POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2. Public: the gallery and a page that doesn't exist (404 {"error": "not_found"}, never 401)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/published

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/published/no-such-page-2099

### 3. Without X-Origin: expect 403 {"error": "origin_rejected"}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}

### 4. Create a page: 201 with "slug": null and "version": 0

# @name createPage
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "HTTP test 2099",
  "description": "Created by api/ui-builder.http",
  "course": "csp",
  "spec": {
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "kind": "ocs-ui-page",
    "page": { "title": "HTTP test 2099", "description": "Created by api/ui-builder.http", "byline": "", "course": "csp", "width": "contained", "image": "" },
    "sections": [
      { "id": "s-http2099", "type": "stack", "settings": {}, "hidden": false,
        "cells": [ { "blocks": [
          { "id": "b-http2099", "type": "hero", "settings": { "title": "HTTP test 2099", "lead": "Made by the REST Client." }, "hidden": false },
          { "id": "b-hidden99", "type": "callout", "settings": { "body": "Hidden, so the published copy leaves it out." }, "hidden": true }
        ] } ] }
    ]
  }
}

### 5. Your pages and groups

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages?scope=mine
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/my-groups
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client

### 6. Save version 0: the answer has "version": 1

# @name savePage
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "title": "HTTP test 2099 (saved)",
  "spec": {
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "kind": "ocs-ui-page",
    "page": { "title": "HTTP test 2099 (saved)", "description": "Created by api/ui-builder.http", "byline": "", "course": "csp", "width": "contained", "image": "" },
    "sections": [
      { "id": "s-http2099", "type": "stack", "settings": {}, "hidden": false,
        "cells": [ { "blocks": [
          { "id": "b-http2099", "type": "hero", "settings": { "title": "HTTP test 2099 (saved)" }, "hidden": false }
        ] } ] }
    ]
  }
}

### 7. Save version 0 again, as a second tab would: 409 version_conflict with currentVersion 1

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "spec": { "schemaVersion": 1, "kind": "ocs-ui-page", "page": { "title": "Stale tab" }, "sections": [] }
}

### 7b. "Keep mine" from that tab: save over version 1 with newRevision, so the answer has "version": 2
# and request 12 lists two SAVE revisions (the copy it replaced stays in Revisions).

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1,
  "newRevision": true,
  "title": "HTTP test 2099 (kept)",
  "spec": {
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "kind": "ocs-ui-page",
    "page": { "title": "HTTP test 2099 (kept)", "description": "Created by api/ui-builder.http", "byline": "", "course": "csp", "width": "contained", "image": "" },
    "sections": [
      { "id": "s-http2099", "type": "stack", "settings": {}, "hidden": false,
        "cells": [ { "blocks": [
          { "id": "b-http2099", "type": "hero", "settings": { "title": "HTTP test 2099 (kept)" }, "hidden": false }
        ] } ] }
    ]
  }
}

### 8. A spec with a script: 400 invalid_spec with details [{"nodeId": "b-bad2099", "field": "body", "key": "bad_body"}]

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 2,
  "spec": { "schemaVersion": 1, "kind": "ocs-ui-page", "page": { "title": "Bad" },
    "sections": [ { "id": "s-bad2099", "type": "stack", "settings": {}, "hidden": false,
      "cells": [ { "blocks": [ { "id": "b-bad2099", "type": "text", "settings": { "body": "<script>alert(1)</script>" }, "hidden": false } ] } ] } ] }
}

### 9. Publish version 2 with a new slug (each run gets its own): status PUBLISHED, publishedVersion 2

# @name publishPage
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/publish
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 2,
  "slug": "http-test-2099-{{$timestamp}}"
}

### 10. The published page (signed in), and the gallery

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/published/{{publishPage.response.body.$.slug}}

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/published?course=csp

### 11. The editing lease: take it, then give it back (204)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/lease
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/lease
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

### 12. Revisions, newest first (SAVE and PUBLISH rows), and whether a slug is free

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/revisions
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/slug-available?slug={{publishPage.response.body.$.slug}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client

### 13. Make it public. A teacher or admin approves the published version they reviewed for everyone,
# so they send its publishedVersion; anyone else only asks (and publishedVersion is ignored).

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/visibility
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "publishedVersion": {{publishPage.response.body.$.publishedVersion}}
}

### 13b. A teacher approving a version that isn't the published one (say a publish landed after their
# review): 409 {"error": "published_changed", "publishedVersion": 2}, and nothing changes for visitors

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/visibility
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "publishedVersion": 0
}

### 14. Back to members only, then unpublish

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/visibility
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "visibility": "SIGNED_IN"
}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}/unpublish
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

### 15. Clean up: delete the test page (204), then reading it is 404

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
Content-Type: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ui-builder/pages/{{createPage.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{pagesOrigin}}
X-Origin: client
